:: Widgets DoLX Changelog [widget]
<<widget "DoLXChangelog">>
	<div class="dolx-changelog">
		<div class="dolx-changelog-hero">
			<span class="dolx-changelog-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128220;</span>
			<div>
				<div class="dolx-changelog-label">PATCH NOTES</div>
				<h1>DoL X-Change <span>v0.20.16</span></h1>
				<div class="dolx-changelog-apk-note"><strong>Official X-Change APK:</strong> Join the DoL Modding server and check the dedicated <a href="https://discord.com/channels/675158131688603721/1512272787572785162" target="_blank">X-Change Channel</a>.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<a class="dolx-changelog-release-link" href="https://gitgud.io/Akoz/dol-xchange/-/releases" target="_blank"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128279;</span> View the full changelog and all releases <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon new" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Changes and Additions</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Added Harper NNPC vanilla sprites by saturdayat11</strong><ul>
		<li>Currently supports the male, white-skin version only.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added painkiller medication</strong><ul>
		<li>The hospital pharmacy now sells packs of 14 painkillers for <strong>£15</strong>.</li>
		<li>Painkillers provide strong pain relief but cause considerable tiredness.</li>
		<li>The school medicine cabinet now shows <strong>&quot;Steal painkillers&quot;</strong> beneath <strong>&quot;Break in.&quot;</strong></li>
		<li>A successful theft gives 3 pills and uses the cabinet's existing weekly restock.</li>
		<li>Painkillers can always be taken while you own them, but taking too many in one day causes increasingly severe side effects:<ul>
		<li><strong>Doses 1-3:</strong> Normal effects.</li>
		<li><strong>Doses 4-5:</strong> Increasing nausea, stress, tiredness, and recovery time.</li>
		<li><strong>Doses 6-7:</strong> Stronger dizziness, trauma, pain, tiredness, and awareness loss.</li>
		<li><strong>Dose 8 onward:</strong> Severe reactions that worsen with each additional dose.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>The daily dose count resets through the existing pill system.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Whitney event: Night Shenanigans</strong><ul>
		<li>Whitney may now visit your orphanage window at night once per week by throwing pebbles at it.</li>
		<li>This event becomes available after the special orphanage visit where Whitney reaches maximum lust and barges into the orphanage.</li>
		<li>You can spend the night vandalising the town with Whitney or share a quieter night together.</li>
		<li>A hidden route lets you leave Whitney, then later apologise and make up with them in the park.</li>
		<li>After making up, Whitney can visit again for a one-time event where they give you a <strong>Water Dragon plushie</strong>.</li>
		<li>The plushie can be carried or placed in several safe locations, including the orphanage, Eden's cabin, the temple bunk, and the Great Hawk tower.</li>
		<li>Sleeping beside the plushie reduces trauma.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added a school hallway follow-up to Whitney's vandalism route</strong><ul>
		<li>After taking part in the vandalism route during Night Shenanigans, other students may notice what you did and admire it.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Water Dragon egg laying and the Hidden Nest</strong><ul>
		<li>At <strong>Water Dragon transformation stage 7</strong>, when you are pregnant, your body producing eggs.</li>
		<li>When an egg is ready, an instinctive pull leads you from the beach through an underwater opening in the sea wall to a hidden nesting hollow.</li>
		<li>Bailey cannot follow you inside.</li>
		<li>Ordinary transformation eggs can be laid at the nest, carried away, and sold to Harper.</li>
		<li>Rare pastel-coloured eggs sell for more.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Hidden Nest restoration</strong><ul>
		<li>Cleaning the nesting hut increases its habitability and permanently unlocks new features:<ul>
		<li><strong>15%:</strong> Usable bed.</li>
		<li><strong>30%:</strong> Tide pool mirror.</li>
		<li><strong>45%:</strong> Dry clothes chest and full wardrobe.</li>
		<li><strong>70%:</strong> Sheltered cooking fire.</li>
		<li><strong>100%:</strong> Search the hidden shore for shells and coral to decorate the wall.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Harper's Water Dragon research route: Project Pelagos</strong><ul>
		<li>Selling four eggs to Harper makes them take a much stronger interest in your transformation.</li>
		<li>After the fourth sale, you can be confined in a secure basement research wing beneath the hospital.</li>
		<li>Each day contains four research sessions, which can include fertility serum, brooding, examinations, and assessments.</li>
		<li>Between sessions, you can use the washroom or spend time in the day room.</li>
		<li>There are two main ways to leave:<ul>
		<li><strong>Cooperate:</strong> Follow Harper's instructions until they decide naturally laid eggs are more useful and release you under a permanent egg-selling arrangement.</li>
		<li><strong>Escape:</strong> Investigate the ventilation system, earn Professor Vale's trust, and use their help to attempt an escape through the service area.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Being caught during an escape attempt costs progress and causes Harper to increase security.</li>
		<li>Leaving the lab by either route grants <strong>Accelerated Brood Cycle</strong>, permanently reducing the time between eggs by roughly half.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added special clothing: Tidebloom Ring</strong><ul>
		<li>During Project Pelagos, you can secretly grow lilies in a hidden tray behind the day room shelf.</li>
		<li>Whether you are released or escape, you leave with one flower woven into the <strong>Tidebloom Ring</strong>.</li>
		<li>While worn:<ul>
		<li>People are more likely to notice you.</li>
		<li><strong>Dendrophile</strong> and <strong>Nectar Addict</strong> no longer decrease over time.</li>
		<li>The Traits menu shows when the ring is preventing those traits from fading.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>Gwylan has unique dialogue about the ring, with different reactions depending on how you left Project Pelagos.</li>
		<li>Afterwards, the ring can be bought from the forest shop or unlocked through a feat boost.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Androgynous Appearance and Clothing Preferences</strong><ul>
		<li>You can now choose <strong>Androgynous</strong> as your preferred Appearance and Clothing style alongside Masculine and Feminine.</li>
		<li>Androgynous preferences have their own acceptance, rejection, and dysphoria effects.</li>
		<li>This is separate from <strong>&quot;Don't Care,&quot;</strong> which disables clothing preference effects.</li>
		<li>Clothing dysphoria now judges your overall outfit instead of each item separately, so mixed masculine and feminine clothing may balance out.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Arousal Acclimated trait</strong><ul>
		<li>Staying Lustful for two full weeks, or already having <strong>Chastity Acclimated</strong>, can unlock <strong>Arousal Acclimated</strong>.</li>
		<li>The trait halves all arousal gained and allows you to sleep even at extremely high arousal.</li>
		<li>It also prevents high arousal from forcing several actions, such as keeping you in the bath or shower or preventing you from leaving certain encounters.</li>
		<li>The trait can be enabled or disabled in game settings.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added optional virginity loss from sex toys</strong><ul>
		<li>Added <strong>&quot;Toys can take virginity&quot;</strong> under <strong>Settings &gt; Sex Toys</strong>.</li>
		<li>The option is <strong>off by default</strong>.</li>
		<li>When enabled, insertable toys can take vaginal or anal virginity when used by an enemy, by the player, or on an NPC.</li>
		<li>The <strong>Math Dildo</strong> school incident now follows this setting. When disabled, you pull away before it can take your virginity.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Mastery Traits</strong><ul>
		<li>Reaching <strong>SSS rank in two related skills</strong> can now unlock a named Mastery Trait with a unique bonus.</li>
		<li>Mastery Traits appear in a new section at the bottom of the Traits screen.</li>
		<li>Combat Masteries improve attacks or evasion and include <strong>Rock 'Em, Sock 'Em</strong>, <strong>Precise Blows</strong>, <strong>Sleek and Steady</strong>, and <strong>Happy Feet</strong>.</li>
		<li>Intimacy Masteries improve specific techniques or body-part interactions and include <strong>Milky Goddess</strong>, <strong>That Cannot Fit!</strong>, <strong>Abyssal Throat</strong>, <strong>Tender Hands</strong>, <strong>Sweet Pleasure</strong>, and <strong>Backend Beauty</strong>.</li>
		<li><strong>Happy Feet</strong> upgrades and replaces <strong>Sleek and Steady</strong> instead of stacking with it.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Fear Toxin spiking and an anti-pill</strong><ul>
		<li><strong>Fear Toxin</strong> is a new optional X-Change spiking effect.</li>
		<li>While active, it keeps trauma at maximum and self-control at zero.</li>
		<li>When it ends, trauma and self-control recover normally rather than being restored instantly.</li>
		<li>Fear Toxin is disabled by default and can be enabled or adjusted under <strong>Spiking Preferences</strong>.</li>
		<li>It cannot appear together with Innocence because the two effects alter trauma in opposite directions.</li>
		<li>The shady park dealer can now sell an <strong>SWP Anti-Feartoxin Pill</strong>, which ends the toxin early but causes the usual anti-pill hypersensitivity.</li>
		<li>The dealer will no longer offer the same two anti-pills on consecutive days.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Bear Prints event</strong><ul>
		<li>Players with <strong>Deviancy 4</strong> can follow bear prints if beast content is enabled and the bear is allowed by their settings.</li>
		<li>Following the prints leads to the bear's hollow and a <strong>hard Willpower check</strong>.</li>
		<li>Enough Bear transformation progress lets you skip the check because the bear recognises your scent.</li>
		<li>Passing the check begins the new willing encounter; failing it leads into the existing forced bear encounter.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added more Love Interest milkshake gifts</strong><ul>
		<li>Kylar can now receive milkshakes at the park, manor, and arcade when your relationship is high enough.</li>
		<li>Sydney can now receive one at the temple as well as the school library.</li>
		<li>Kylar's gift option now correctly uses two milkshakes.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated sleeping with Love Interests</strong><ul>
		<li>Robin and Alex can now wake you naturally when sleeping together.</li>
		<li>Each has dedicated wake-up dialogue and lets you either get up or stay in bed and snuggle.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added more modded face slots</strong><ul>
		<li>Modded face slots now extend up to <strong>30</strong>.</li>
		<li>Some slots may be empty unless their graphics are added manually.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Tweaks and Rebalancing</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Body size now affects maximum Dodge Chance</strong><ul>
		<li>Smaller characters can dodge more effectively, with the smallest body size able to reach up to <strong>100% Dodge Chance</strong>.</li>
		<li>Larger characters have a lower limit, with the biggest builds capped at <strong>45%</strong>.</li>
		<li>Average-sized characters are unchanged.</li>
		<li>The <strong>Dodge Chance Cap</strong> setting can still lower your maximum, but it cannot raise it above your body-size limit.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Rebalanced combat damage</strong><ul>
		<li>Punches, kicks, and hook punches no longer multiply every damage bonus together.</li>
		<li>Trained fighters still deal more damage, but attacks now have limits based on the opponent's health.</li>
		<li>Light attacks can deal up to <strong>12%</strong> of the opponent's health, while powerful two-handed attacks can deal up to <strong>40%</strong>.</li>
		<li>Kicks now deal slightly less damage than punches because they remain available while both hands are occupied.</li>
		<li>Sadism no longer increases physical damage, but still affects stress, arousal, and fight reactions.</li>
		<li>Fixed kicks causing later punches to incorrectly use kicking skill for damage.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Transformation income bonuses rebalanced</strong><ul>
		<li>No transformation can double earnings anymore.</li>
		<li>The maximum transformation income bonus is now <strong>75%</strong>.</li>
		<li>This affects larger bonuses such as the cat café, bunny dancing, bear dock work, and Angel temple allowance.</li>
		<li>Smaller bonuses, such as bird and cow jobs, are unchanged.</li>
		<li>Minor cosmetic traits such as Seraphim eyes, Kitsune cheeks, or small Okami features no longer count as a complete transformation by themselves.</li>
		<li>A defining feature such as wings, ears, or a tail is now required for full transformation benefits for chimera.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Chastity arousal now depends on consent and key control</strong><ul>
		<li>Chastity no longer builds frustration simply because you are wearing it.</li>
		<li>Frustration now builds when the device was forced on you, someone else controls the key, the key was lost or stolen, or the device became impossible to remove.</li>
		<li>Temple chastity no longer causes frustration because you willingly asked Jordan to lock it.</li>
		<li>Self-locked chastity does not cause frustration, even with Lustful traits, although Lustful can still increase arousal normally.</li>
		<li>Self-bought dildo chastity belts now correctly stimulate you regardless of who controls the key.</li>
		<li>Wearing chastity continuously for 10 days grants <strong>Chastity Acclimated</strong>, permanently reducing frustration from chastity.</li>
		<li>The chance of losing a carried key has been reduced in scenes where it can break, be stolen while you are unconscious, or be taken after losing a fight.</li>
		<li>Temple chastity devices are no longer incorrectly marked as stolen after loading a save, and affected saves repair automatically.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Clearer Innocence and Drunkenness action hints</strong><ul>
		<li>Skill requirements such as <strong>&quot;Exhibitionism 4&quot;</strong> now visually show when Innocence or drunkenness is letting you qualify.</li>
		<li>The requirement glows when high Innocence lets you act without understanding the risk.</li>
		<li>The requirement sways when you are drunk enough to ignore it.</li>
		<li>Choosing a risky action through Innocence now slightly lowers Innocence, with more dangerous actions costing more.</li>
		<li>Fixed Exhibitionism and Deviancy scenes using Promiscuity instead of the correct stat when deciding whether to show oblivious text.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Apologising in combat now depends on English grade</strong><ul>
		<li>Poorly worded apologies begin at roughly <strong>30%</strong> of their previous calming strength.</li>
		<li>Their effect improves with English grade and reaches full strength at the highest grade.</li>
		<li>Angry reactions from characters who refuse to forgive you are unchanged.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Reworked the school hallway pantsing event</strong><ul>
		<li>The event can now happen only once per day.</li>
		<li>Allowing it to happen pulls down your bottoms without automatically tearing your clothing.</li>
		<li>Students laughing at you lowers school standing, and mismatched underwear can cause rumours.</li>
		<li>You can now elbow the attacker using <strong>Physique</strong> instead of Athletics.</li>
		<li>Success makes them back off; failure makes the encounter rougher and can tear clothing.</li>
		<li>Helping pull down your own bottoms ends the struggle quickly but causes the largest reputation loss.</li>
		<li>Trying to grab your bottoms still uses Athletics.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>&quot;Submit&quot; foot action updated</strong><ul>
		<li>Because Submit only makes you drop to your knees, it now remains available while bound, shackled, grappled, or entangled.</li>
		<li>You must still be standing, not pinned against a wall, and in a non-consensual encounter.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Improved blackmail handling</strong><ul>
		<li>Blackmail letter delivery has been improved.</li>
		<li>Ignored letters can now be forwarded to the orphanage for one week.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Poppy availability</strong><ul>
		<li>Poppy is no longer accessible again after dismissal.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated the DECOMOD interface</strong><ul>
		<li>The <strong>Updated UI</strong> option now includes a redesigned DECOMOD tab layout.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Various narrative and pacing cleanup</strong><ul>
		<li>Tidied pacing and wording in several scenes.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Fixes and Improvements</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Fixed X-Change bodies sharing virginity records</strong><ul>
		<li>Your original, X-Change, herm, and cloned bodies now keep separate virginity records.</li>
		<li>Taking another Premium pill while already transformed no longer makes the game forget which body you are using.</li>
		<li>Taking another pill while cloned no longer loses the copied identity or saves virginity changes to the wrong body.</li>
		<li>Cloned bodies now have their own virginity records instead of inheriting another body's history.</li>
		<li>Older saves will preserve their existing original-body history instead of losing it when a pill wears off.</li>
		<li>After a clone pill ends, the game no longer continues treating you as the copied person.</li>
		<li>Pills used on NPCs now restore the NPC's body correctly instead of accidentally loading the player's body.</li>
		<li>Virginity changes made through cheats, the Testing Room, or brothel re-virgining now save to the body currently in use.</li>
		<li>Existing saves may still contain older virginity changes that were already recorded on the wrong body, but new changes will no longer become mixed.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Body Size and Slow Change Progress</strong><ul>
		<li>X-Change pills now handle body size and slow transformations correctly.</li>
		<li><strong>Swell</strong> only increases body size while the effect is active, and normal size returns when it ends even if you take another pill or swap bodies.</li>
		<li>The temporary penis-size increase from Alpha pills has also been fixed.</li>
		<li>Slow body-change progress no longer resets to <strong>0%</strong>.</li>
		<li>Pregnancy, ear slime, or changes to your sense of self pause progress instead, and it resumes from the same point later.</li>
		<li>Existing saves with an already incorrect stored body size cannot be repaired automatically, but the size will correct itself the next time that body is stored.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed X-Change combat descriptions</strong><ul>
		<li>X-Change pills no longer break enemy descriptions during combat.</li>
		<li>Transformed enemies keep the correct body description, name, and pronouns instead of showing <strong>&quot;undefined&quot;</strong> or raw code.</li>
		<li>Enemies using male pronouns while having breasts are now described correctly.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed X-Change whoring protection</strong><ul>
		<li>The street-whoring event now checks all forms of pill protection.</li>
		<li>The stranger will no longer approach while you are protected by Harper's therapy or X-Change Purity.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed divine transformations stacking effects</strong><ul>
		<li>Only one divine form can now be mechanically active at a time, prioritising <strong>Demon</strong>, then <strong>Fallen Angel</strong>, then <strong>Angel</strong>.</li>
		<li>Lower-priority divine limbs remain visible as cosmetic parts but no longer grant overlapping skills, buffs, income bonuses, or other transformation effects.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed dysphoria Willpower and Stress handling</strong><ul>
		<li>Rejected dysphoria now drains current Willpower instead of permanently training it.</li>
		<li>Begrudged traits now correctly increase Stress and Trauma without also granting preferred-trait relief.</li>
		<li>Identity comfort bonuses have been reduced.</li>
		<li>The Statistics screen now displays Begrudged traits correctly.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Whitney temperature dialogue</strong><ul>
		<li>Whitney will no longer complain that <strong>&quot;it is too hot&quot;</strong> in math class when the temperature is cold or below zero.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed wardrobe crashes and invalid clothing choices</strong><ul>
		<li>Wardrobes no longer mistake location requirements for clothing.</li>
		<li>Invalid wardrobe choices, such as trying to equip a bathrobe after bathing, are now ignored instead of deleting the entire clothing slot and breaking later screens.</li>
		<li>Existing saves remove malformed or misplaced wardrobe entries on load while preserving valid clothing and temporary scene storage.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed kaiju costume unlocks and wardrobe duplicates</strong><ul>
		<li>Borrowed costumes from Niki's flyer job no longer trigger automatic clothing rebuy or become stranded in the wardrobe.</li>
		<li>Existing costume stacks are repaired.</li>
		<li>Older saves regain the forest shop and Gwylan unlocks where appropriate.</li>
		<li>Over-outfit management is now exposed correctly.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed clothing issues during combat</strong><ul>
		<li>The <strong>Undress</strong> menu no longer errors when an NPC has nothing removable on a body part.</li>
		<li>Newly equipped clothing no longer inherits the pulled-up or pulled-down state of the previous item.</li>
		<li>This also prevents some NPCs, especially with ModLoader clothing, from repeatedly attempting the same failed clothing action every turn.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed worn strap-ons</strong><ul>
		<li>Removing a strap-on during combat or somewhere without a wardrobe no longer duplicates it or leaves it marked as worn.</li>
		<li>Removed strap-ons now return to the toy inventory correctly.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed adult shop chastity handling</strong><ul>
		<li>Unpaid chastity items can no longer be kept for free.</li>
		<li>Returning clothing or being caught leaving without paying also removes unpaid chastity items.</li>
		<li>Buying and wearing a new chastity item now stores the old one instead of deleting it.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed adult shop help-work timing</strong><ul>
		<li>The setup scene no longer appears at inappropriate times such as 1 a.m.</li>
		<li>It is now available only from <strong>noon to 9 p.m.</strong> on the correct days.</li>
		<li>Outside those hours, the shop stays boarded up as normal.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Bailey paid-date prices</strong><ul>
		<li>Spanking, cat ears, dinner, and overnight options now all use the same price shown in the menu.</li>
		<li>Fixed related formatting issues.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Bailey option disappearing after the spanking scene</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Jordan being misgendered</strong><ul>
		<li>Corrected Jordan's pronouns in the Street Monstrance scene.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed the Ivory Wraith missing from the Social tab</strong><ul>
		<li>Escaping its first possession attempt or being possessed while sleeping now correctly counts as meeting the Wraith.</li>
		<li>Existing saves repair automatically when loaded.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed money exploits and limits</strong><ul>
		<li>Dice bets can no longer use negative values to create money.</li>
		<li>Bailey's deposit and withdrawal inputs now correctly limit the amount you can enter, including while in debt.</li>
		<li>The dice table now has a weekly spending limit of <strong>£10,000</strong>.</li>
		<li>Once reached, Landry closes the table until the following week because the amount of money has become too noticeable.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed and rebalanced the dice game</strong><ul>
		<li>Fixed a bug where an unwon pot could be returned without being emptied, allowing the same money to be won again later.</li>
		<li>Going all-in no longer makes opponents fold almost every time.</li>
		<li>Bets are capped at the table's buy-in, and the wager box shows how much more you can bet.</li>
		<li>The special ending for defeating every opponent can now trigger correctly.</li>
		<li>Winnings are rounded to whole pennies.</li>
		<li>If two players run out of money in the same round, both leave the table correctly.</li>
		<li>Every drink on the penalty tray now has an equal chance of being spiked.</li>
		<li>Kiss and clothing-removal options no longer appear when no opponents remain.</li>
		<li>Leaving while acting as the shooter now takes five minutes, matching other exit methods.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed bike cooldowns</strong><ul>
		<li>Stolen bikes take <strong>10 in-game days</strong> to return before day 150 and <strong>7 days</strong> from day 150 onward.</li>
		<li>Major bike-breaking events use a separate shared <strong>10-day cooldown</strong> across town, forest, and open-road events.</li>
		<li>Bike cooldowns now decrease correctly each day and disappear at zero.</li>
		<li>Interrupted rides no longer award workout gains left over from an earlier ride.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed rain watering unvisited crop plots</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Fixed smoking at Alex's farm</strong><ul>
		<li>Smoking no longer teleports you outside.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed dual contact lenses at the pharmacy</strong><ul>
		<li>Custom eye colours now correctly let you choose separate left and right colours.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed sleeping crashes on fresh browser data</strong><ul>
		<li>The game now creates missing Hopeless Cycle browser-storage data before trying to read it.</li>
		<li>This prevents crashes on new devices, fresh browser profiles, or after clearing site data.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed daily options becoming permanently unavailable</strong><ul>
		<li>Daily, weekly, and monthly resets now run separately.</li>
		<li>An error in one reset can no longer prevent the others from running.</li>
		<li>Reset errors are recorded in the error console instead of being silently hidden.</li>
		<li>Existing saves repair affected options the next time a new day begins.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed the Flats dog event</strong><ul>
		<li>The event now restores and identifies the human resident before displaying their description.</li>
		<li>If they cannot be found, the scene uses the neutral phrase <strong>&quot;the resident&quot;</strong> and continues normally.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed sale price estimates</strong><ul>
		<li>Journal prices and Winter's dialogue now include the Divine Transformation income bonus.</li>
		<li>Displayed estimates now match the actual payout.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed &quot;your naked&quot; text</strong><ul>
		<li>Fixed several scenes where characters could interact with clothing the player was not wearing.</li>
		<li>If you are already topless during the <strong>Pants Down</strong> or <strong>Expose</strong> events, the text now correctly refers to your bare chest instead of using broken lines such as <strong>&quot;pulls up your naked.&quot;</strong></li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed missing RNG in the temple</strong></li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Mastery combat state</strong><ul>
		<li>Using a hook punch once no longer makes every later attack in the fight easier for the opponent to dodge.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Feat cleanup</strong><ul>
		<li>Removed feats that were redundant or unobtainable in DoLX.</li>
		<li><strong>God of Lust</strong> now requires maximum tempered Oral and Hand skill instead.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Various small bug fixes and cleanup</strong></li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="dolx-changelog-section-icon images" aria-hidden="true">&#128444;</span> Art and Image Updates</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Updated GooseFem and GooseMasc by snowy</strong><ul>
		<li>See the Goose community thread for additional details.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Mysterious by MJ</strong><ul>
		<li>Added cow ears and eyeswings.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
<</widget>>
